title: Fortios: IPSec
agents: special
catalog: network/fortigate
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the IPSec tunnels of a Fortigate firewall.
 All tunnels are monitored by default.
 The "fortios_ipsec_discovery" rule can be used to exclude entire tunnels
 from discovery using regular expressions matched against the service name
 (e.g. "IPSec Tunnel VDOM root MyTunnel").
 The "fortios_ipsec_check_parameters" rule can be used to configure the 
 tunnels ignored by name and remote subnet, using regular expressions
 (partial match) instead of exact names.
 A tunnel is displayed as {crit} if it is not active.


 The special agent is required for this check, 
 which can be configured via “FortiOS”.

discovery:
 One service per IPSec tunnel is created.
